KG42.register("clusters-2d27878822c2fc09cbb3e063",{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v142-d-K001","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","label":"Rolling bids and centralized reception specifications for multi-energy-carrier commodities","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Rolling bids and centralized reception specifications for multi-energy-carrier commodities","market_meaning":"Trading commodities are distinguished by energy carrier and delivery period. Agents submit and update supply and demand bids to the operator according to the listed format and rolling timing, and comply with the restrictions of divisibility and of cross-hour result conditions. This cluster assembles the commodity definition, the bid requirements already made explicit, and the reception interface.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Hourly submission applies to the 1 h implementation in the text and cannot be extended to a fixed arrangement for every period length. Full time-domain coverage refers to the agent's set of bids and does not require supply and demand bids to be submitted simultaneously every hour. Prohibition of cross-hour result conditions is not equivalent to prohibition of cross-hour bid dependence; different energy carriers remain different commodities.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The energy-carrier and period division of a commodity directly determines the bid fields and the period-by-period submission method, and the bid specification in turn joins the operator's reception duty, forming a submission rule that can be interpreted independently. Optimal allocation, price generation, and settlement have their primary attribution in other clusters, respectively.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Bears the primary attribution of the demand-bid format, submission and updating, and the formal restrictions already listed."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplements the supply-side bid format, rolling submission, and formal restrictions, retaining its local role, which differs from that of the demand side."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Defines the energy carrier, the period commodity, and the energy-carrier suitability range to which a bid refers."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cites only the interface for centralized reception of bids and the standard format; the primary attribution of continuous operation, the independence preference, and result notification lies in v142-d-K002."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The source text defines energy carrier and period as the dimensions that distinguish commodities, and explicitly requires bids to be submitted by period; the demand-bid fields and submission timing obtain their commodity scope on this basis, and no new scientific edge is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The same commodity division also applies to supply bids; time-domain coverage and period-by-period submission complement each other, but do not create an obligation to provide a supply bid every hour."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The demand-side submission action and the central operator's reception of bids at the specified time and in the standard format constitute the same information-delivery interface."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The supply-side submission specification joins the operator's reception duty; the basis of the connection is an explicit bid-transfer relationship."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"All are occurrences of the demand-bid submission node in the same mechanism; the representative citation is used only for display, and all original chain objects are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"All point to the supply-bid submission node of the same mechanism, and the supply and demand nodes are not merged."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence used by this cluster remains unverified; experimental candidate status does not mean that the transcription or the scientific content has received independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The source and applicability conditions are to be checked manually afterward; this round retains only the candidate assembly and does not change source_status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G002","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Bid format, bid dependence, and the rolling time domain still have no approved dedicated nodes; the existing submission chain carrying the related content is not equivalent to these proposals having been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E017"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:bid-format","proposal:bid-dependency","proposal:trading-horizon"],"required_work":"Manually assess the proposal boundaries and the required upstream bindings; before approval, continue to use the frozen citations and do not insert new nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R001 explicitly carries the permission for linked dependence of demand bids, and R002 has no corresponding supply-side submission clause. The general statement in E017 cannot be directly rewritten by D as a new supply-side constraint, so this cluster does not yet cover a complete supply-dependence submission interface.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E018"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:bid-dependency"],"required_work":"The upstream is to make explicit the submission scope and representation of supply-side dependence, and then the corresponding chain content is to be supplemented; the current format and timing candidates keep their established scope."}]},"rule_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R001","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R008","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-853f64cb73659614","KG40-4a0e4a04a308d0b9","KG40-72006c4bf7355110","KG40-80b56ab23344a0b7","KG40-91eceef212419ef6"]});
